   "source": [
    "# Tutorial 5 - Conversion"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "2bad687e-a1f7-4ede-936a-f82befed4561",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "usage: CG2AT2 [-h] [-info] [-version] [-c FILE] [-a [FILE ...]] [-ff NAME]\n",
      "              [-fg [NAME ...]] [-w MODEL] [-o {all,align,de_novo,none}]\n",
      "              [-loc FOLDER] [-d [CHAIN:COPIES ...]] [-group [0,1 ...]] [-ter]\n",
      "              [-nt] [-ct] [-cys DIST] [-silent] [-mod] [-sf FACTOR] [-ov DIST]\n",
      "              [-swap [RULE ...]] [-box LEN LEN LEN] [-vs] [-disre] [-gmx EXE]\n",
      "              [-posre RESNAME] [-compare FILE.itp] [-messy] [-v]\n",
      "\n",
      "CG2AT2: fragment-based back-mapping of coarse-grained systems to atomistic resolution.\n",
      "Requires a GROMACS installation. Full documentation: https://github.com/owenvickery/cg2at\n",
      "\n",
      "options:\n",
      "  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n",
      "  -info                 Print available force fields and fragment libraries,\n",
      "                        then exit.\n",
      "  -version              show program's version number and exit\n",
      "\n",
      "input files:\n",
      "  -c FILE               Coarse-grained input structure (required).\n",
      "  -a [FILE ...]         Atomistic input structure(s). Supplying the original\n",
      "                        atomistic file improves conversion quality. Multiple\n",
      "                        files are accepted.\n",
      "\n",
      "force field and fragment library:\n",
      "  -ff NAME              Force field to use, e.g. charmm36-jul2022. If omitted,\n",
      "                        CG2AT2 will prompt interactively.\n",
      "  -fg [NAME ...]        Fragment library (or libraries, in priority order),\n",
      "                        e.g. martini_2-2_charmm36. If omitted, CG2AT2 will\n",
      "                        prompt interactively.\n",
      "  -w MODEL              Water model to use, e.g. tip3p, tip4p, spc, spce. If\n",
      "                        omitted, CG2AT2 will prompt interactively.\n",
      "\n",
      "output:\n",
      "  -o {all,align,de_novo,none}\n",
      "                        Controls which final structures are produced (default:\n",
      "                        all). none – minimised de novo structure only, no MD\n",
      "                        de_novo – as \"none\" plus a short 5 ps NVT run align –\n",
      "                        minimised de novo morphed to the user structure via\n",
      "                        steered MD all – both de_novo and align outputs\n",
      "  -loc FOLDER           Name of the output folder. Default: CG2AT_<timestamp>.\n",
      "                        Re-using an existing folder lets you resume a failed\n",
      "                        run.\n",
      "\n",
      "protein chains:\n",
      "  -d [CHAIN:COPIES ...]\n",
      "                        Duplicate atomistic chains. Format: CHAIN:COPIES\n",
      "                        [CHAIN:COPIES ...]. Example: \"0:3 1:3\" creates 3\n",
      "                        copies of chains 0 and 1.\n",
      "  -group [0,1 ...]      Treat atomistic chains as rigid bodies during fitting.\n",
      "                        Provide comma-separated chain indices per group,\n",
      "                        separated by spaces, e.g. \"0,2 1,3\". Use \"all\" to fit\n",
      "                        the entire structure as one body, or \"chain\" to group\n",
      "                        by CG chain.\n",
      "  -ter                  Interactively choose N- and C-terminal capping groups\n",
      "                        for each chain.\n",
      "  -nt                   Apply a neutral N-terminus to all chains.\n",
      "  -ct                   Apply a neutral C-terminus to all chains.\n",
      "\n",
      "disulphide bonds:\n",
      "  -cys DIST             Maximum S–S distance (Å) for disulphide bond detection\n",
      "                        (default: 7). Increase if bonds are missed; Martini\n",
      "                        S–S distances can reach ~10 Å.\n",
      "  -silent               Automatically accept all detected disulphide bonds\n",
      "                        without prompting.\n",
      "\n",
      "conversion tuning:\n",
      "  -mod                  Treat every fragment bead independently rather than\n",
      "                        fitting grouped beads together. Grouping is on by\n",
      "                        default and generally gives better geometry.\n",
      "  -sf FACTOR            Scale factor applied to fragments before fitting\n",
      "                        (default: 0.9, i.e. 90%). Reducing this lowers the\n",
      "                        chance of atom clashes before minimisation.\n",
      "  -ov DIST              Minimum allowed distance between atoms (Å) before\n",
      "                        overlap is flagged (default: 0.3).\n",
      "  -swap [RULE ...]      Swap residues or beads during conversion. Format:\n",
      "                        FROM[,BEAD]:TO[,BEAD][:RESID_RANGE]. Example:\n",
      "                        \"POPC,NC3:POPG,GL0\" or \"ASP:ASN:0-10,30-40\". Use\n",
      "                        \"skip\" as the target to remove a residue or bead\n",
      "                        entirely.\n",
      "  -box LEN LEN LEN      Override the periodic box dimensions (Å, cubic boxes\n",
      "                        only). Supply three values; use 0 to preserve the\n",
      "                        original size on that axis. Example: \"-box 100 100 0\"\n",
      "                        resizes X and Y only.\n",
      "  -vs                   Add virtual sites to protein hydrogen atoms.\n",
      "  -disre                Apply a backbone H-bond distance restraint matrix\n",
      "                        during NVT (requires -a; on by default when an\n",
      "                        atomistic structure is supplied).\n",
      "\n",
      "utilities:\n",
      "  -gmx EXE              GROMACS executable to use (default: gmx). Set this if\n",
      "                        you have multiple GROMACS versions installed, e.g.\n",
      "                        gmx_avx.\n",
      "  -posre RESNAME        Generate a position restraint .itp file for the named\n",
      "                        non-protein residue, then exit.\n",
      "  -compare FILE.itp     Compare all residues in an .itp file against the\n",
      "                        fragment database, then exit.\n",
      "  -messy                Keep all temporary files after the run (useful for\n",
      "                        debugging).\n",
      "  -v                    Increase output verbosity. Stack up to three times\n",
      "                        (-vvv) for maximum detail.\n",
      "\n",
      "Examples:\n",
      "  Minimal:    cg2at.py -c system.gro\n",
      "  Recommended: cg2at.py -c system.gro -a protein.pdb\n",
      "  Automated:  cg2at.py -c system.gro -a protein.pdb -ff charmm36-jul2022 -fg martini_2-2_charmm36 -w tip3p\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "!cg2at_lite -h"
   ]
  },
